    {
      "id": 4984,
      "status": "Verified",
      "type": "Technical",
      "section": "5.2.10, appA",
      "date": "2017-03-30",
      "orig": "Each bit represents an Information Element in the Data Record\nwith the n-th bit\nrepresenting the n-th Information Element.",
      "correct": "Each bit represents an Information Element in the Data Record,\nwith the n-th least significant bit\nrepresenting the n-th Information Element.",
      "notes": "A misunderstand arose as to whether bits were assigned in host order or network order - so clarify that the bits are assigned from the least significant to the most significant, ie right-to-left rather than left-to-right.\n\nMoreover, this clarification applies to IANA's IPFIX registry.\n\nNB RFC 8038 re-uses this definition for mibIndexIndicator. Consistency between the definitions is desirable."
    }
